place my order, and it's ready in the 6 minutes it takes me to get there. Best part? Order a \"Combo\" and you get a dressed cheeseburger, crinkle fries, and a can soda for $7. The kitchen in the back of this store is small, nothing fancy, but always clean and efficient. The older gentleman that worked the kitchen was a true gentleman, was a master at cooking up anything back there in no time flat, and had the tendency to share off-menu foods that he had prepared for free (my favorite were his grape leaves). Sad..."},{"business_id":"0169EQn9SEi1bocoX5Ps1w","review_id":"ssfXiOGlKFwj_HsXB9w-Ug","date":"2013-01-25T18:03:47","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.8861016631126404,"text_excerpt":"The reason we stopped in to this little neighborhood place was for the pecan beer. We would definitely go back, if we were in the area again. Friendly place, good prices, good selection."},{"business_id":"0169EQn9SEi1bocoX5Ps1w","review_id":"WfaFsLIiut4GRvUELqAtGQ","date":"2017-02-16T19:43:49","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.876460611820221,"text_excerpt":"If you see a guy grilling outside this place during Mardi Gras, get the cheeseburger. The cheeseburgers here are delicious and I definitely recommend. This place is also great for all your adult beverage needs. What else could you ask for?"}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
